WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.234
Welcome to Building Defender XDR,

2
00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:06.212
a developer workbook in the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

3
00:00:06.212 --> 00:00:09.438
This is Chapter 5: exposure and incidents.

4
00:00:09.438 --> 00:00:12.872
A vulnerability without an
owner is an inventory finding,

5
00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:15.876
and an incident without an
owner is a clock running.

6
00:00:15.876 --> 00:00:19.788
Both checks in this chapter ask
the same question: who has this?

7
00:00:19.788 --> 00:00:23.813
We'll start from the guide's queries
and Learn's incident list, and the

8
00:00:23.813 --> 00:00:26.976
government-cloud fact that
shapes the exposure gate,

9
00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:29.276
then read both checks and walk two labs.

10
00:00:29.276 --> 00:00:31.908
The chapter is a draft awaiting review;

11
00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:35.420
the code is illustrative,
tested against fixtures.
